# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what the service imports or reads at run time.
# deploy/Dockerfile copies `core` as a whole, so this file alone decides what is in the image. A path
# listed here that does not exist yet is simply absent. Later lines win. A module outside these
# packages that they import (core/answer_text.py, shared by the answer pipeline and the eval) is
# listed by name, here and in the completeness check of deploy/remote-deploy.sh.
*
!core/requirements.txt
!core/app/
!core/tools/
!core/agent/
!core/bills/
!core/answer_text.py
!core/metrics/*.sql
!core/config/*.yaml
!core/knowledge/*.yaml
# of the sample bills (#249) only the images and samples.json are served: no PDFs, no README
core/bills/samples/*.pdf
core/bills/samples/README.md

# never in the image: tests, caches
**/tests/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
